---
// About masthead — the page opens like a magazine feature (same grammar as
// D's Meet Lauren spread): giant serif question, then the approved one-line
// answer. The hook is the manifesto's decided line; the dek is the approved
// headline lift from the one-pager. Cream ground, so the nav rides red.
---

<section class="fc-abt-masthead" id="about" aria-labelledby="abt-title" data-nav-cream>
  <h1 id="abt-title" data-rv style="--rvi: 0">
    Who said kid play had to be <em>imaginary?</em>
  </h1>

  <p class="dek" data-rv style="--rvi: 1">
    STAND is where kids build <strong>real businesses</strong> and
    <strong>real-life skills</strong> &mdash; the modern day lemonade stand.
  </p>
</section>

<style>
  .fc-abt-masthead {
    background: var(--stand-cream);
    color: var(--stand-black);
    max-width: calc(1132px + 2 * 48px);
    margin: 0 auto;
    /* Top clears the fixed nav; bottom hands off to Our approach on the
       same cream ground, so it stays tighter than a section seam. */
    padding: clamp(128px, 14vw, 192px) 48px clamp(40px, 4.4vw, 64px);
  }

  /* Feature-opener scale — same red-serif magazine voice as the Meet Lauren
     spread, question set in black with the payoff word flipped red italic
     (the hero's "For Real." emphasis grammar). */
  h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: clamp(40px, 6vw, 92px);
    line-height: 1.02;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    max-width: 14ch;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  h1 em {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--stand-red);
  }

  .dek {
    margin: clamp(20px, 2.2vw, 32px) 0 0;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(17px, 1.6vw, 23px);
    line-height: 1.5;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    max-width: 48ch;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .dek strong {
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .fc-abt-masthead {
      padding-left: 20px;
      padding-right: 20px;
    }
  }
</style>
